1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,110
When you go on holiday, where do you like to stay?
度假时，你喜欢住在哪里？

2
00:00:04,110 --> 00:00:14,140
Do you like the luxury of a five-star hotel, the convenience of a self-catering apartment or do you prefer the freedom of sleeping under canvas?
是偏爱五星级酒店的奢华、自助公寓的便利，还是更向往睡在帐篷里的无拘无束？

3
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:22,360
If you haven’t tried the latter, maybe you should join the increasing number of people who are enjoying the simple pleasures of camping.
如果你还没试过最后一种，或许你应该像越来越多的人一样，去体验露营带来的简单乐趣。

4
00:00:22,360 --> 00:00:31,920
By grabbing your tent, and some additional accessories, it’s easy to head off to the countryside and enjoy a night or two under the stars.
带上帐篷和一些附加装备，很容易就可以前往郊外，在星空下度过一两晚。

5
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:48,230
Many campers are ditching the trappings of their modern, hectic life to do this, encouraged by experts who say a few peaceful nights in the middle of nowhere might be a good way to unwind and improve our sleep patterns and well-being.
许多露营爱好者都会抛开现代快节奏生活的繁琐羁绊，选择这样的休闲方式。专家也表示，在偏远宁静的地方度过几个平和的夜晚，或许是放松身心、改善睡眠规律与身心健康的好办法。

6
00:00:48,230 --> 00:00:53,160
It is also, of course, a good low-budget holiday option.
当然，这也是一种低成本的度假选择。

7
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:58,910
For the adventurous, wild camping is the ultimate escape from reality.
对于热爱冒险的人来说，野外露营是逃离现实的终极方式。

8
00:00:58,910 --> 00:01:08,940
Armed with just some food and a sleeping bag, you’re free from rules, away from other people, and able to enjoy the back-to-basics experience.
只带上些许食物和一个睡袋，你就能摆脱规则，远离人群，享受这种回归本真的体验。

9
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:22,220
One wild camper, Phoebe Smith, told the BBC: “The act of sleeping when everybody else has gone home – when you notice the wildlife and the stars – is one of the best things in life.”
野外露营爱好者菲比·史密斯在接受BBC采访时说：“当所有人都已归家，你却在户外入眠——留意着周围的野生动物和满天繁星，这是生活中最美好的事情之一。”

10
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:29,680
But for those who still want some home comforts, a campsite is a more suitable place to pitch your tent.
但对于那些仍想保留一些居家舒适的人来说，露营地会是更适合搭帐篷的地方。

11
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:35,970
Here you have facilities such as washrooms, a shop and maybe even a restaurant.
这里有洗手间、小卖部，甚至可能有餐厅之类的设施。

12
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:41,320
And for the most luxurious camping experience, you could try glamping.
而如果想体验最奢华的露营，你可以试试“精致露营”。

13
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:46,460
In the UK, camping – and caravanning – has always been popular.
在英国，露营以及房车旅行向来十分受欢迎。

14
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:54,990
One survey by Visit Britain found around 4.38 million people go camping in Britain every year.
英国旅游局的一项调查显示，每年约有438万人会在英国本土露营。

15
00:01:54,990 --> 00:02:07,620
More recently, sales of camping gear have jumped as more people have opted for a staycation within the UK due to travel restrictions caused by the coronavirus pandemic.
近年来，受新冠疫情引发的旅行限制影响，更多人选择在英国境内度假，露营装备的销量也随之猛增。

16
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:16,890
One camping retailer, Halfords, reported a surge in demand for products such as stoves, cool boxes and camping chairs.
露营用品零售商哈福德公司报告称，炉具、冷藏箱和露营椅这类产品的需求激增。

17
00:02:16,890 --> 00:02:33,160
With the addition of inflatable mattresses and pillows, powerful torches and lamps to light up your tent and a better selection of easy-to-cook food, you can almost guarantee a comfortable and enjoyable camping expedition.
有了充气床垫和枕头、能照亮帐篷的强光手电筒与灯具，再加上种类更丰富的易于烹饪的食材，你几乎能确保拥有一次舒适愉悦的露营之旅。

18
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:38,080
The only thing you can’t guarantee, in the UK at least, is good weather!
不过有一件事是无法保证的——至少在英国是这样——那就是晴朗的好天气！

19
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:42,800
So maybe it’s time to slum it and give camping a try.
所以，或许是时候放下精致，去体验一次露营了。
